  "note_markdown": "### ZION — Earnings normalize after an unusually strong second quarter\n\n**Reported GAAP diluted EPS declined to $1.78 from $3.05 in 2Q26**, a $1.27 sequential decline. Net earnings applicable to common shareholders fell to $262 million from $452 million [B0239, B0248]. The comparison is distorted by the prior quarter's significantly higher noninterest income [B0242].\n\n**EPS drivers:** Current-quarter earnings included a $10 million credit valuation adjustment gain on client-related swaps, equivalent to $0.05 per share. Excluding that disclosed gain would lower the indicated underlying contribution, but the bank did not provide a comprehensive adjusted diluted EPS measure [B0033].\n\n**Revenue and margin:** GAAP NII increased $7 million to $684 million, while FTE NIM contracted 4 basis points to 3.23%. Noninterest income fell to $197 million from $460 million, and expenses increased modestly to $553 million from $551 million [B0059, B0064, B0242, B0243].\n\n**Credit:** Provision was an $8 million benefit versus a $3 million expense in 2Q26. Net charge-offs fell to $3 million, representing an exceptionally low annualized ratio of 0.02%. ACL coverage was 1.11% [B0246, B0041, B0264, B0265].\n\n**Capital and returns:** CET1 stood at 11.8%, reported ROTCE was 16.2%, and tangible book value totaled $43.50 per share. Share repurchases were $75 million [B0271, B0258, B0251, B0187].\n\n**Outlook:** Management projected 8%–12% NII growth and 2%–4% period-end loan growth for 3Q27 versus 3Q26, alongside positive expected operating leverage [B0788].\n\n**Investment thesis:** Broadly intact. Quarterly EPS normalization is substantial, but improving loan growth expectations and subdued credit losses support the forward outlook."
